SHIGUR, Iraq — Authorities in Iraq’s Nineveh Governorate have announced plans to accelerate reconstruction in Shigur (Sinjar / Shengal), including compensation for destroyed homes and the integration of Sinjar Protection Units (YBŞ) fighters into official security and civilian institutions. Nineveh Governor Abdul Qader al-Dakhil announced the measures from Mount Shigur, describing the integration process as &hellip;
Al-Dakhil also announced plans to transform the Sinjar Reconstruction Fund into an independent entity, in coordination with relevant authorities and the United Nations, to accelerate reconstruction projects and improve essential services.
However, authorities have not disclosed the budget allocated for compensation, the number of households eligible for assistance, or a timeline for payments.

